    "created_at": "2023-04-14T19:15:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-14T19:15:25Z",
    "body": "> Yeah it would be very easy to just set _fireEvents_ to false in the attribute change steps\r\n\r\nHmm, I'm a bit concerned about adding another case that doesn't fire events. But I suppose we already do that when the *element* is removed from the DOM, and removing/changing the *attribute* could be considered similar to that. But kind of less-so.\r\n\r\nI'm still trying to wrap my head around why in [the example](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/11326#discussion_r1151531770) the second popover has manual behavior. Can you help me understand that? I'm wondering if we couldn't just check for this case after the `beforetoggle` fires and reset the state appropriately.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
